; ================================================================
;  GUAIACOL / CREOSOL explicit sub-block  --  SAPHFIRE migration  (DRAFT for review)
;  Replaces the crude guaiacol/creosol -> CATECHOL injection surrogate.
;
;  SOURCES
;    guaiacol+OH branching : Evans/Nienhouse et al., ACS ES&T Air 2026 (PMC13077636), optimized Scheme 1
;    downstream 4-nitrocatechol : Finewax, de Gouw & Ziemann 2018, ES&T 52:1981 (catechol+OH 0.30 / +NO3 0.91)
;    k(NO3) : Yang et al. 2016, Atmos. Environ. (guaiacol 3.2e-12, creosol 2.4e-13)
;    k(OH)  : Lauraguais et al. 2014 (guaiacol ~7.5e-11)   [PIN exact at integration]
;    k(O3)  : El Zein 2015 ~4e-19  -> NEGLIGIBLE, omitted on purpose
;
;  DESIGN = "minimal explicit": methoxy-aromatics kept as distinct species (so the fix REDUCES
;  rather than RELOCATES the nitro-catechol SOA); only genuine MCM-twins migrated immediately
;  (CATECHOL, GLYOX, MGLYOX, MALDIAL, MCATECHOL + their existing MCM downstream chemistry).
;
;  *** FLAGGED ESTIMATES (need your sign-off) are marked [EST] ***
;   [EST-1] guaiacol+OH product split is chamber-OPTIMIZED (not measured); nitroguaiacol 16% is
;           folded into the OH reaction => hard-codes a high-NOx dependence (OK for SAPHIR NOx).
;   [EST-2] OMCATECHOL nitration fate (-> OMNCATECHOL) has NO literature yield; modelled on the
;           MCM MCATECHOL template (k~2e-10). This is the key SOA brown-carbon former.
;   [EST-3] whole CREOSOL block is by-analogy to guaiacol (no measured creosol OH split).
;   [EST-4] C* / volatility of the NEW condensers (OMCATECHOL, OMNCATECHOL, NGUAIACOL,
;           OMPBZQONE, NCREOSOL) -> to be set in make_volatility_tsv.py before the SOA scheme.
;
;  NEW SPECIES (formula for volatility / mass):
;    GUAIACOL   C7H8O2   | CREOSOL     C8H10O2   (precursors)
;    OMCATECHOL C7H8O3   (3-methoxycatechol, 48% branch, condensable)
;    OMCATEC1O  C7H7O3   (methoxycatechol-oxy radical)
;    OMNCATECHOL C7H7NO5 (methoxy-nitrocatechol -- main SOA, [EST-2])
;    NGUAIACOL  C7H7NO4  (4-/6-nitroguaiacol, condensable)
;    OMPBZQONE  C7H6O3   (2-methoxy-1,4-benzoquinone, condensable)
;    GUAIAOXMUC C7H8O4   (methoxy epoxide/muconaldehyde, ring-opening precursor)
;    GUAIAO2    C7H9O5   (guaiacol OH-adduct peroxy radical)
;    OMMCATECHOL C8H10O3 (methoxy-methylcatechol, creosol analog, condensable)
;    NCREOSOL   C8H9NO4  (6-nitrocreosol, condensable)
;  MIGRATED to existing MCM species: CATECHOL, NCATECHOL(+radicals), GLYOX, MGLYOX, MALDIAL,
;    MCATECHOL, MNCATECH  (all confirmed present in full MCM v3.3.1)
; ================================================================

; ---------------- MECH ----------------
; --- Guaiacol primary (OH dominant; O3 omitted) ---
GUAIACOL  +  OH   -->  0.482*OMCATECHOL + 0.16*NGUAIACOL + 0.179*GUAIAOXMUC + 0.119*GUAIAO2 + 0.06*CATECHOL + 0.60*HO2
GUAIACOL  +  NO3  -->  NGUAIACOL + HNO3

; --- Guaiacol peroxy / ring-opening (alkoxy fragmentation, quinone:dicarbonyl = 70:30) ---
GUAIAO2   +  NO   -->  NO2 + 0.70*OMPBZQONE + 0.30*MALDIAL + 0.30*MGLYOX + GLYOX + HO2
GUAIAOXMUC +  OH  -->  GLYOX + MGLYOX + HO2

; --- Methoxycatechol (the 48% branch): MCM-catechol-style nitration ---
OMCATECHOL +  OH   -->  OMCATEC1O
OMCATECHOL +  NO3  -->  OMCATEC1O + HNO3
OMCATEC1O  +  NO2  -->  OMNCATECHOL

; --- Small catechol branch (6%) uses EXISTING MCM catechol chemistry (already in mech) ---
;   CATECHOL + OH/NO3 -> ... -> NCATECHOL  (unchanged, now fed only 6% not 100%)

; --- Creosol primary (by analogy [EST-3]) ---
CREOSOL   +  OH   -->  0.482*OMMCATECHOL + 0.16*NCREOSOL + 0.179*GUAIAOXMUC + 0.119*GUAIAO2 + 0.06*MCATECHOL + 0.60*HO2
CREOSOL   +  NO3  -->  NCREOSOL + HNO3
; methoxy-methylcatechol shares the methoxycatechol oxidation chemistry (lumped to save species)
OMMCATECHOL +  OH   -->  OMCATEC1O
OMMCATECHOL +  NO3  -->  OMCATEC1O + HNO3
;   6% MCATECHOL branch uses EXISTING MCM chemistry -> MNCATECH (unchanged)

; ---------------- RATE ----------------
k[GUAIACOL+OH-->0.482*OMCATECHOL+0.16*NGUAIACOL+0.179*GUAIAOXMUC+0.119*GUAIAO2+0.06*CATECHOL+0.60*HO2]=CONST(7.53D-11)
k[GUAIACOL+NO3-->NGUAIACOL+HNO3]=CONST(3.2D-12)
k[GUAIAO2+NO-->NO2+0.70*OMPBZQONE+0.30*MALDIAL+0.30*MGLYOX+GLYOX+HO2]=CONST(2.7D-12*EXP(360/(T)))
k[GUAIAOXMUC+OH-->GLYOX+MGLYOX+HO2]=CONST(1.0D-11)
k[OMCATECHOL+OH-->OMCATEC1O]=CONST(2.0D-10)
k[OMCATECHOL+NO3-->OMCATEC1O+HNO3]=CONST(1.7D-10)
k[OMCATEC1O+NO2-->OMNCATECHOL]=CONST(2.08D-12)
k[CREOSOL+OH-->0.482*OMMCATECHOL+0.16*NCREOSOL+0.179*GUAIAOXMUC+0.119*GUAIAO2+0.06*MCATECHOL+0.60*HO2]=CONST(7.5D-11)
k[CREOSOL+NO3-->NCREOSOL+HNO3]=CONST(2.4D-13)
k[OMMCATECHOL+OH-->OMCATEC1O]=CONST(2.0D-10)
k[OMMCATECHOL+NO3-->OMCATEC1O+HNO3]=CONST(1.7D-10)

; ---------------- INJECTION ----------------
; DONE in a NEW file (original left untouched):
;   E:/Python Code/JUICE archive/EASY/include files/saphfire_injection.guaiacol.incl
; Solution-A Q_A lump   0.197429*CATECHOL   ->  0.102037*GUAIACOL + 0.042300*CREOSOL + 0.053086*CATECHOL
; (fractions = 4.231 / 1.754 / 2.201 ppb over the 41.4653 ppb solution-A total).
; Load saphfire_injection.guaiacol.incl INSTEAD OF saphfire_injection.incl, together with this block.
